    "about": "post by a small business owner, or job post",
    "kinds": {
      "pain": "Describes a problem in running the business that keeps coming back or costs real time or money: a chore done by hand, a tool that fails or costs too much, a rule or deadline that is hard to meet, a workaround. A bad review of a paid business app that says what it fails to do counts.",
      "chore-job": "A job post paying someone to do a recurring business chore by hand: bookkeeping, data entry, reconciling, copying between systems, scheduling, chasing invoices or customers, managing listings.",
      "build-job": "A job post for one-off work: building a website, app or software, design, video, writing, marketing, sales, or a salaried role.",
      "question": "A one-off question or request for advice, with no recurring problem behind it: how to start, which to choose, is this legal, feedback on my store.",
      "promo": "Selling or promoting something: the poster's own product, service, agency or store, or a survey or 'what are your pain points' post from someone building a product.",
      "other": "Anything else: news, celebration, venting about a customer, a rant with no problem to solve, a consumer's personal question, off topic."
    },
    "drop": ["build-job", "promo", "other"]
  }
